ions missing transverse momentum through the requirement of the online lepton reconstructed by the trigger being within ΔR=0.1 of an off-line reconstructed lepton.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6 + Body ¶7 + Body ¶8 + Body ¶9", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events are selected by a combination of single electron or muon triggers for each data-taking period [ 82 , 83 , 84 , 85 ] , and the online lepton reconstructed by the trigger is required to be within ΔR=0.1 [ 86 ] of an off-line reconstructed lepton.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions that events are selected by a combination of single electron or muon triggers, indicating a search, and it also mentions missing transverse momentum through the requirement of the online lepton reconstructed by the trigger being within ΔR=0.1 of an off-line reconstructed lepton.\"}\n```"}]}
{"qid": "gf-05", "paper_id": "2205.05120", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The invariant mass of the system m is a key variable for separating H candidate events from the background in this analysis.", "answers": [], "votes": {"True": 3}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": ["The CMS detector + Event selection"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2205.05120", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": true, "quote": "The invariant mass of the system m is a key variable for separating H candidate events from the background in this analysis.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions reconstructing the invariant mass of the system m for separating H candidate events.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Event selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The invariant mass of the system m is a key variable for separating H candidate events from the background in this analysis.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions reconstructing the invariant mass of the system m for separating H candidate events.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2205.05120", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": true, "quote": "The invariant mass of the system m is a key variable for separating H candidate events from the background in this analysis.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions reconstructing the invariant mass of the system m, which is a key variable for separating H candidate events from the background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Event selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The invariant mass of the system m is a key variable for separating H candidate events from the background in this analysis.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions reconstructing the invariant mass of the system m, which is a key variable for separating H candidate events from the background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2205.05120", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": true, "quote": "This algorithm reconstructs h candidates based on the number of tracks and the number of ECAL strips with energy deposits within the associated η - φ plane and reconstructs one-prong, one-prong+ 0 (s), and three-prong decay modes (where a “prong” refers to a charged hadron constituent).", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text explicitly mentions reconstructing h candidates, which are Higgs-boson candidates.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Event selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"This algorithm reconstructs h candidates based on the number of tracks and the number of ECAL strips with energy deposits within the associated η - φ plane and reconstructs one-prong, one-prong+ 0 (s), and three-prong decay modes (where a “prong” refers to a charged hadron constituent).\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions reconstructing h candidates, which are Higgs-boson candidates.\"}\n```"}]}
