{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2206.09466", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The uncertainty in the b tagging efficiency is modeled by implementing seventeen nuisance parameters, five of which are related to the theoretical uncertainties involved in the measurements and are therefore correlated among the three data sets. The remaining four parameters per data set, which arise from the statistical accuracy of the efficiency measurement, are kept uncorrelated [ 31 ] . These uncertainties have an impact on both the shape of the templates and their normalization for all the simulated samples.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 45, "True": 3}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Abstract + Introduction", "Data sets and simulations", "Different-flavor ${\\mathup{{{V}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ 2j categories + Same-flavor ${\\mathup{{{V}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}$ 2j categories + The STXS measurement + Background estimation", "Different-flavor VBF categories + Same-flavor VBF categories + Vector boson associated production categories", "Different-flavor ggH categories", "Event selection and categorization", "Event selection and categorization + Gluon fusion categories", "Multiboson background", "Nonprompt lepton background + Top quark background + Nonresonant ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}{\\mathup{{{W}}}}$ background + Drell–Yan background", "Same-flavor ggH categories + Vector boson fusion categories", "Statistical procedure and systematic uncertainties", "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "WHSS categories + WH3 $\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}$ categories", "ZH3 $\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}$ categories + ZH4 $\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}$ categories"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2206.09466", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search using b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 0, "escalated": fal