rise from the statistical accuracy of the efficiency measurement, are kept uncorrelated [ 31 ] . These uncertainties have an impact on both the shape of the templates and their normalization for all the simulated samples.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions b-tagged jets.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Statistical procedure and systematic uncertainties", "window": 13, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The uncertainty in the b tagging efficiency is modeled by implementing seventeen nuisance parameters, five of which are related to the theoretical uncertainties involved in the measurements and are therefore correlated among the three data sets. The remaining four parameters per data set, which arise from the statistical accuracy of the efficiency measurement, are kept uncorrelated [ 31 ] . These uncertainties have an impact on both the shape of the templates and their normalization for all the simulated samples.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2206.09466", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": true, "quote": "The uncertainty in the $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ tagging efficiency is modeled by implementing seventeen nuisance parameters, five of which are related to the theoretical uncertainties involved in the measurements and are therefore correlated among the three data sets.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions the use of b-tagged jets.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Statistical procedure and systematic uncertainties", "window": 13, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The uncertainty in the $\\\\mathup{{{b}}}$ tagging efficiency is modeled by implementing seventeen nuisance parameters, five of which are related to the theoretical uncertainties involved in the measurements and are therefore correlated among the three data sets.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions the use of b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2206.09466", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": true, "quote": "The uncertainty in the b tagging efficiency is modeled by implementing seventeen nuisance parameters, five of which are related to the theoretical uncertainties involved in the measurements and are therefore correlated among the three data sets. The remaining four parameters per data set, which arise from the statistical accuracy of the efficiency measurement, are kept uncorrelated [ 31 ] . These uncertainties have an impact on both the shape of the templates and their normalization for all the simulated samples.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Statistical procedure and systematic uncertainties", "window": 13, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The uncertainty in the b tagging efficiency is modeled by implementing seventeen nuisance parameters, five of which are related to the theoretical uncertainties involved in the measurements and are therefore correlated among the three data sets. The remaining four parameters per data set, which arise from the statistical accuracy of the efficiency measurement, are kept uncorrelated [ 31 ] . These uncertainties have an impact on both the shape of the templates and their normalization for all the simulated samples.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum.\"}\n```"}]}
