{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2308.02285", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "A normalization factor of 0.92 ± 0.02 is required to bring into agreement data and t¯t simulation. The uncertainty in the background normalization factors reflects the statistical uncertainty of the data and the simulations in the control samples.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 5, "True": 1}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": ["Event selection in the SL channel", "The CMS detector + Object reconstruction + Event selection"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2308.02285", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention b-tagged jets.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Object reconstruction + Event selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2308.02285", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention b-tagged jets", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Object reconstruction + Event selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention b-tagged jets\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2308.02285", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Object reconstruction + Event selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The analysis follows the selection strategy used in Ref. [ 8 ] and requires the presence of a high- $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ isolated lepton in the region $\\lvert\\eta^{\\ell}\\rvert<2.4$ and $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\ell}>35\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ .\", \"why\": \"The quote shows that the analysis is a search for events with a high-pT isolated lepton, which is a common selection criterion in searches for new physics.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2308.02285", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SL channel", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Additionally demanding at least three high- $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ jets, two of which are tagged as ${\\mathup{{{b}}}}$ jets\", \"why\": \"The text specifies that the event selection includes b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2308.02285", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SL channel", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"A normalization factor of $0.92\\pm 0.02$ is required to bring into agreement data and ${{\\mathup{{{t}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}}$ simulation. The uncertainty in the background normalization factors reflects the statistical uncertainty of the data and the simulations in the control samples. Once the absolute normalization of the ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}+\\text{jets}$ and ${{\\mathup{{{t}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}}$ background contributions are determined, the ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}+\\text{jets}$ simulation is scaled so that the sum of the events from all predicted contributions be equal to the number of events in the selected data sample. The normalization factor of the ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}+\\text{jets}$ simulation (0.95) has only a minor effect in the contribution of the (small) predicted ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}+{{\\mathup{{{u}}}}{\\mathup{{{d}}}}{\\mathup{{{s}}}}{\\mathup{{{g}}}}}$ background. The overall normalization of the ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}+{\\mathup{{{c}}}}$ signal simulation is irrelevant for the analysis, since it is only used for acceptance and efficiency calculations.\",\"why\": \"The text mentions a search for ${{\\mathup{{{t}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}+\\text{jets}$ backgrounds, which requires b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2308.02285", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": true, "quote": "A normalization factor of 0.92 ± 0.02 is required to bring into agreement data and t¯t simulation. The uncertainty in the background normalization factors reflects the statistical uncertainty of the data and the simulations in the control samples.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions b-tagged jets in the context of event selection.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SL channel", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"A normalization factor of 0.92 ± 0.02 is required to bring into agreement data and t¯t simulation. The uncertainty in the background normalization factors reflects the statistical uncertainty of the data and the simulations in the control samples.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions b-tagged jets in the context of event selection.\"}\n```"}]}
