 false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"In the SRs, the two highest $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ leptons are also required to have the same flavor, ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{}{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ or ${\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ , while for a number of CRs we require the presence of different-flavor (DF) leptons, ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\pm}}}}{}{}^{\\mp}$ .\", \"why\": \"The text mentions b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum in the event selection criteria.\"}\n```"}]}
