{"qid": "gf-07", "paper_id": "2006.05880", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The number of events with fake/non-prompt leptons is estimated with the data-driven technique described in Section Fake/non-prompt lepton background.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 2, "True": 1}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": ["Background estimation + Fake/non-prompt lepton background + Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson background in the 3 $\\ell$ selection"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Background estimation + Fake/non-prompt lepton background + Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson background in the 3 $\\ell$ selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The normalisation of the main backgrounds ( $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson in the $3\\ell$ selection; $t\\bar{t}$ in the $1\\ell$ selection) is obtained by fitting the yield from MC simulation to the observed data in dedicated control regions (CRs) enhanced in a particular background component, and then extrapolating this yield to the SRs.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions the use of control regions to normalise the ttZ background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Background estimation + Fake/non-prompt lepton background + Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson background in the 3 $\\ell$ selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The background from fake/non-prompt (FNP) leptons is estimated in a data-driven way, while the normalisation of the main backgrounds ( $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson in the $3\\ell$ selection; $t\\bar{t}$ in the $1\\ell$ selection) is obtained by fitting the yield from MC simulation to the observed data 