{"qid": "gf-05", "paper_id": "2604.27044", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "In the resolved event topology, CMS set observed (expected) upper limits at the 95% CL on the signal strength μHH of 3.9 (7.8); constraints were also set on κλ , with the bounds found to be −2.3<κλ<9.4 (−5.0<κλ<12.0).", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 12, "True": 3}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Abstract", "Introduction", "Large-radius jet flavor identification and mass reconstruction + Event selections", "The CMS detector + Object and event reconstruction + The L1 selection", "The HLT selection + Small-radius jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ reconstruction"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Object and event reconstruction + The L1 selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Object and event reconstruction + The L1 selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Object and event reconstruction + The L1 selection", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object selected on.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The HLT selection + Small-radius jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object selected on.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The HLT selection + Small-radius jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention reconstructing a Higgs-boson candidate as a physical object.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "The HLT selection + Small-radius jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The invariant mass distributions of the reconstructed $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ -leading ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}_{1}$ ) and subleading ( ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}_{2}$ ) $\\mathup{{{H}}}$ candidates in simulated SM ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}{\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to 4{\\mathup{{{b}}}}$ events are shown in Fig. 4 (left), with and without application of the regression.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions the invariant mass distributions of reconstructed Higgs candidates.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Large-radius jet flavor identification and mass reconstruction + Event selections", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To select ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ candidates from offline AK8 jets and reconstruct their mass, the global particle transformer ( GloParT ) algorithm [ Qu:2022mxj , CMS:2026uph ] is used.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly states that the analysis uses the GloParT algorithm to reconstruct the mass of Higgs-boson candidates.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Large-radius jet flavor identification and mass reconstruction + Event selections", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To select ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ candidates from offline AK8 jets and reconstruct their mass, the global particle transformer ( GloParT ) algorithm [ Qu:2022mxj , CMS:2026uph ] is used.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly states that the analysis reconstructs the mass of Higgs-boson candidates.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Large-radius jet flavor identification and mass reconstruction + Event selections", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To select ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ candidates from offline AK8 jets and reconstruct their mass, the global particle transformer ( GloParT ) algorithm [ Qu:2022mxj , CMS:2026uph ] is used.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions reconstructing the mass of Higgs-boson candidates.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events in which the Higgs boson decays, ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ , are separately reconstructed as pairs of small-radius jets (resolved), as well as those where they are reconstructed as single large-radius jets (merged), are studied exclusively.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions that events with Higgs boson decays are reconstructed.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events in which the Higgs boson decays, ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ , are separately reconstructed as pairs of small-radius jets (resolved), as well as those where they are reconstructed as single large-radius jets (merged), are studied exclusively.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly states that events where the Higgs boson decays are reconstructed.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events in which the Higgs boson decays, ${\\mathup{{{H}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ , are separately reconstructed as pairs of small-radius jets (resolved), as well as those where they are reconstructed as single large-radius jets (merged), are studied exclusively.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions the reconstruction of Higgs boson decays.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": true, "quote": "In the resolved event topology, CMS set observed (expected) upper limits at the 95% CL on the signal strength μHH of 3.9 (7.8); constraints were also set on κλ , with the bounds found to be −2.3<κλ<9.4 (−5.0<κλ<12.0).", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The quote shows that the analysis sets constraints on κλ, which is the coupling modifier for the Higgs boson self-coupling, indicating that the analysis reconstructs Higgs-boson candidates.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Introduction", "window": 1, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"yes\",\n  \"quote\": \"In the resolved event topology, CMS set observed (expected) upper limits at the 95% CL on the signal strength μHH of 3.9 (7.8); constraints were also set on κλ , with the bounds found to be −2.3<κλ<9.4 (−5.0<κλ<12.0).\",\n  \"why\": \"The quote shows that the analysis sets constraints on κλ, which is the coupling modifier for the Higgs boson self-coupling, indicating that the analysis reconstructs Higgs-boson candidates.\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": true, "quote": "The primary challenge of the searches in the 4 b channel is separating the H H signal from the overwhelming background and precisely modeling the background contribution in the analysis regions.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The analysis reconstructs Higgs boson candidates as physical objects it selects on.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Introduction", "window": 1, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The primary challenge of the searches in the 4 b channel is separating the H H signal from the overwhelming background and precisely modeling the background contribution in the analysis regions.\", \"why\": \"The analysis reconstructs Higgs boson candidates as physical objects it selects on.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2604.27044", "qid": "gf-05", "answer": true, "quote": "In the resolved event topology, CMS set observed (expected) upper limits at the 95% CL on the signal strength μHH of 3.9 (7.8); constraints were also set on κλ , with the bounds found to be −2.3<κλ<9.4 (−5.0<κλ<12.0).", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions setting upper limits on the signal strength μHH, which implies reconstructing Higgs-boson candidates.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Introduction", "window": 1, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"In the resolved event topology, CMS set observed (expected) upper limits at the 95% CL on the signal strength μHH of 3.9 (7.8); constraints were also set on κλ , with the bounds found to be −2.3<κλ<9.4 (−5.0<κλ<12.0).\", \"why\": \"The text mentions setting upper limits on the signal strength μHH, which implies reconstructing Higgs-boson candidates.\"}\n```"}]}
{"qid": "gf-07", "paper_id": "2008.05928", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The dominant SM background arises from events with prompt photons produced in association with jets ( γ +jets). Less dominant SM backgrounds include a prompt photon produced in association with a W/Z boson ( W/Z + γ ) or a top–anti-top quark pair ( t t ¯ + γ ).", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 1, "True": 2}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6 + Body ¶7"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2008.05928", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6 + Body ¶7", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The dominant SM background arises from events with prompt photons produced in association with jets ( $\\gamma$ +jets). Less dominant SM backgrounds include a prompt photon produced in association with a $W/Z$ boson ( $W/Z$ + $\\gamma$ ) or a top–anti-top quark pair ( $t\\bar{t}$ + $\\gamma$ ).\", \"why\": \"The text mentions ttZ background as a less dominant SM background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2008.05928", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "The dominant SM background arises from events with prompt photons produced in association with jets ( γ +jets). Less dominant SM backgrounds include a prompt photon produced in association with a W/Z boson ( W/Z + γ ) or a top–anti-top quark pair ( t t ¯ + γ ).", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions t t ¯ + γ as a background.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6 + Body ¶7", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The dominant SM background arises from events with prompt photons produced in association with jets ( γ +jets). Less dominant SM backgrounds include a prompt photon produced in association with a W/Z boson ( W/Z + γ ) or a top–anti-top quark pair ( t t ¯ + γ ).\", \"why\": \"The text mentions t t ¯ + γ as a background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2008.05928", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "The dominant SM background arises from events with prompt photons produced in association with jets ( γ +jets). Less dominant SM backgrounds include a prompt photon produced in association with a W/Z boson ( W/Z + γ ) or a top–anti-top quark pair ( t t ¯ + γ ).", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text lists ttZ as a background.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6 + Body ¶7", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The dominant SM background arises from events with prompt photons produced in association with jets ( γ +jets). Less dominant SM backgrounds include a prompt photon produced in association with a W/Z boson ( W/Z + γ ) or a top–anti-top quark pair ( t t ¯ + γ ).\", \"why\": \"The text lists ttZ as a background.\"}\n```"}]}
