 "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention b-tagged jets\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention b-tagged jets.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic event reconstruction", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic event reconstruction", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Any leptons reconstructed in the event are automatically assigned to the ${\\mathbf{S}}$ system in the event interpretation, while jets and SVs can appear as either coming from sparticles or ISR.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions b-tagged jets (SVs) and missing transverse momentum (pTmiss).\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic event reconstruction", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Any leptons reconstructed in the event are automatically assigned to the ${\\mathbf{S}}$ system in the event interpretation, while jets and SVs can appear as either coming from sparticles or ISR.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions b-tagged jets in the event selection.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic event reconstruction", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Any leptons reconstructed in the event are automatically assigned to the ${\\mathbf{S}}$ system in the event interpretation, while jets and SVs can appear as either coming from sparticles or ISR.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions b-tagged jets\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention missing transverse momentum.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic event reconstruction", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention missing transverse momentum.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention missing transverse momentum.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic event reconstruction", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention missing transverse momentum.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention missing transverse momentum.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic event reconstruction", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention missing transverse momentum.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Depending on the region, there are then further subdivisions according to the number of $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged jets observed in the S and ISR systems (NbS and NbISR)\", \"why\": \"The text mentions that the analysis uses b-tagged jets as part of its event selection.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Depending on the region, there are then further subdivisions according to the number of $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged jets observed in the S and ISR systems (NbS and NbISR), or the number of SVs assigned to S (NsvS), which are further split into SV central and forward categories (svc and svf, respectively).\", \"why\": \"The text mentions that the analysis subdivides events based on the number of b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Depending on the region, there are then further subdivisions according to the number of $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged jets observed in the S and ISR systems (NbS and NbISR)\", \"why\": \"The text mentions that the analysis uses b-tagged jets in the event selection.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 6, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 6, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 6, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"For all of the 2L silver and bronze regions, leptons are separated by flavor ( ${\\mathup{{{e}}}}{\\mathup{{{e}}}}$ , , or ${\\mathup{{{e}}}}{\\mathup{}}$ ) in order to better serve as CRs capable of disentangling the contributions from different nonprompt-lepton sources and processes.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions leptons are separated by flavor for 2L silver and bronze regions.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To look for $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -enriched signals similar to those from top squark pair decays, there are three superbins for low $\\Delta m$ and one for medium $\\Delta m$.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions looking for b-enriched signals, which implies the use of b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To look for $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -enriched signals similar to those from top squark pair decays, there are three superbins for low $\\Delta m$ and one for medium $\\Delta m$.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions looking for b-enriched signals and using superbins.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"One of these low- $\\Delta m$ superbins was defined with only low-momentum SV candidates.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions looking for b-enriched signals and defines superbins with specific criteria, including b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": true, "quote": "Events are selected with significant initial-state radiation (ISR), where the high transverse momentum recoil from the ISR can often lead to measurable missing transverse momentum associated with sparticle decays in compressed scenarios, despite each invisible LSP acquiring only a small momentum in the parent rest frame from the parent sparticle decay.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions selecting events with significant missing transverse momentum and b-tagged jets.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events are selected with significant initial-state radiation (ISR), where the high transverse momentum recoil from the ISR can often lead to measurable missing transverse momentum associated with sparticle decays in compressed scenarios, despite each invisible LSP acquiring only a small momentum in the parent rest frame from the parent sparticle decay.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions selecting events with significant missing transverse momentum and b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions the use of b-tagged jets in the event categorization.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2508.13900", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events are categorized based on their lepton multiplicity, jet multiplicity, number of $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -tagged jets, and kinematic variables sensitive to the sparticle masses and mass splittings.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions that events are categorized based on the number of b-tagged jets.\"}\n```"}]}
