{"qid": "gf-07", "paper_id": "2010.14293", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The CR selections maintain adequate statistical precision while minimising the systematic uncertainties arising from the extrapolation of the CR event yield to estimate the background in the SR.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 4, "True": 2}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": ["Background estimation", "Control regions"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2010.14293", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalize it.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Background estimation", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalize it.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2010.14293", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Background estimation", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2010.14293", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Background estimation", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Top quark pair production, followed by semileptonic decays, in particular $t\\bar{t}\\to b\\bar{b}\\tau\\nu qq^{\\prime}$ (with the $\\tau$ -lepton decaying to hadrons), as well as single-top-quark events, can also generate large $E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ and satisfy the jet and lepton veto requirements.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions ttZ background in the context of top quark pair production.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2010.14293", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "The CR selections maintain adequate statistical precision while minimising the systematic uncertainties arising from the extrapolation of the CR event yield to estimate the background in the SR.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions a control region for ttZ background", "answer_text": "", "section": "Control regions", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The CR selections maintain adequate statistical precision while minimising the systematic uncertainties arising from the extrapolation of the CR event yield to estimate the background in the SR.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions a control region for ttZ background\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2010.14293", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "The CR selections maintain adequate statistical precision while minimising the systematic uncertainties arising from the extrapolation of the CR event yield to estimate the background in the SR.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The quote shows that the CRs are used to estimate the background in the SR, including the ttZ background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Control regions", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The CR selections maintain adequate statistical precision while minimising the systematic uncertainties arising from the extrapolation of the CR event yield to estimate the background in the SR.\", \"why\": \"The quote shows that the CRs are used to estimate the background in the SR, including the ttZ background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2010.14293", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Control regions", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The CRT selections omit the SR selection requirements on $\\Delta\\phi($ j $,\\textbf{\\emph{p}}\\mathrm{{}^{miss}_{T}})$ in both search strategies.\", \"why\": \"This sentence shows that the analysis has a ttZ background and a control region used to normalise that background.\"}\n```"}]}
{"qid": "gf-02", "paper_id": "2004.01678", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "A “modified ABCD estimate” of the total background in the SR is derived using four regions: A , defined by 0.0341<M<0.0524 , expected to contain about 10% of the total background, and 155 GeV<mℓℓj<175 GeV ; B , defined by the mℓℓj requirement of the SR and the M requirement of region A ; C , defined by the M requirement of the SR and the mℓℓj requirement of A ; and D , which is the SR.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 3, "True": 3}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6 + Body ¶7 + Body ¶8 + Body ¶9", "Body ¶10 + Body ¶11 +  + Body ¶12 + Body ¶13 + Body ¶14 + Body ¶15"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2004.01678", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention an ABCD method or any ABCD-style sideband or matrix method.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6 + Body ¶7 + Body ¶8 + Body ¶9", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention an ABCD method or any ABCD-style sideband or matrix method.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.01678", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention an ABCD method, or an ABCD-style sideband or matrix method over independent regions.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6 + Body ¶7 + Body ¶8 + Body ¶9", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention an ABCD method, or an ABCD-style sideband or matrix method over independent regions.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2004.01678", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention an ABCD method, or an ABCD-styl