{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2511.11853", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "In this search, we use an ABCD (matrix) background estimation technique, based on parametric fits to our CRs to smooth statistical fluctuations, employing the light-quark and gluon jet, and electron selections to construct CRs to predict the backgrounds in the muon and b jet enriched SRs.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 16, "True": 2}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Abstract + Introduction", "Background estimation", "Data and simulated samples + Event selection and categorization", "Event selection and categorization", "The CMS detector and event reconstruction"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that this analysis is a search.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not explicitly state that this analysis is a search.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To search for a $\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{Z}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\prime}}}$ boson that decays to muons, with associated $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets, we create dimuon signal regions (SRs) containing at least one b-tagged jet and CRs enhanced with either events containing either electrons, or light-quark, or gluon, jets.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions a search for a Z' boson with b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To search for a $\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{Z}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\prime}}}$ boson that decays to muons, with associated $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets, we create dimuon signal regions (SRs) containing at least one b-tagged jet and CRs enhanced with either events containing either electrons, or light-quark, or gluon, jets.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions creating signal regions with b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and categorization", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To search for a $\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{Z}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\prime}}}$ boson that decays to muons, with associated $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets, we create dimuon signal regions (SRs) containing at least one b-tagged jet and CRs enhanced with either events containing either electrons, or light-quark, or gluon, jets.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions searching for a Z' boson that decays to muons with associated b jets, and creating signal regions containing at least one b-tagged jet.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The search does retain some sensitivity to flavor-universal models. For a sequential-SM [ 33 ] $\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{Z}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\prime}}}$ boson with flavor-universal quark couplings most of the parameter space has already been excluded for masses ranging from 150  GeV to 5.15  TeV [ 34 , 9 , 11 ] . The sensitivity of the search reported here for flavor-universal lepton couplings is reduced because of the use of dielectron control regions (CRs) for the background prediction. This limitation will be described in Section 7 .\", \"why\": \"The analysis is a search for a new neutral gauge boson produced in association with one or more jets where at least one is b tagged, that decays into a pair of muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The search does retain some sensitivity to flavor-universal models. For a sequential-SM [ 33 ] $\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{Z}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\prime}}}$ boson with flavor-universal quark couplings most of the parameter space has already been excluded for masses ranging from 150  GeV to 5.15  TeV [ 34 , 9 , 11 ] . The sensitivity of the search reported here for flavor-universal lepton couplings is reduced because of the use of dielectron control regions (CRs) for the background prediction. This limitation will be described in Section 7 .\", \"why\": \"The analysis searches for a new neutral gauge boson in association with jets, including at least one b-tagged jet, and decaying into a pair of muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The search does retain some sensitivity to flavor-universal models. For a sequential-SM [ 33 ] $\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{Z}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\prime}}}$ boson with flavor-universal quark couplings most of the parameter space has already been excluded for masses ranging from 150  GeV to 5.15  TeV [ 34 , 9 , 11 ] . The sensitivity of the search reported here for flavor-universal lepton couplings is reduced because of the use of dielectron control regions (CRs) for the background prediction. This limitation will be described in Section 7 .\", \"why\": \"The analysis is a search for a new neutral gauge boson produced in association with jets, including at least one b-tagged jet, and decaying into a pair of muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not explicitly state that the analysis is a search.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2511.11853", "qid": "gf-01", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that this analysis is a search.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector and event reconstruction", "window": 1, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not explicitly state that this analysis is a search.\"}\n```"}, {