{"qid": "gf-01", "paper_id": "2405.18661", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The analysis relies on MVAs for discriminating the signal process from the backgrounds. A combined fit to the MVA output distributions in the categories of different jet and b jet multiplicities yields a measurement with an uncertainty of about 45% in the signal strength, corresponding to an observed significance of 2.5 s.d. with 1.1 s.d. expected.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 86, "True": 1}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Abstract + Contents + Introduction + The LHC and CMS", "Additional differential measurements of jet production cross sections + Proton PDFs + Overview of CMS constraints on PDFs + The PDF constraints from jet production measurements", "Diboson production", "Differential measurements of vector boson production", "Double-parton scattering + Summary of QCD measurements + Measurements in the electroweak sector of the standard model", "Electroweak single-boson and multiboson production + Summary of EW measurements", "Electroweak top quark production", "Event simulation and cross section calculation", "Event simulation and cross section calculation + Measurements of quantum chromodynamics", "Inclusive differential jet production cross section measurements + Exclusive differential measurements of jet production cross sections + Inclusive $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ -flavoured jet production", "LHC operations, energies, and luminosities", "Measurements of vector boson production in association with heavy-flavour jets + Inclusive multiboson production and interactions", "Measurements of vector boson production in association with jets", "Single weak boson production", "The CMS detector", "The strong coupling constant, $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{S}}$ , and its running", "Top quark measurements", "Total inelastic cross sections + Jet production cross section measurements + Inclusive fiducial jet production cross section measurements", "Triboson production", "Vector boson p