{"qid": "gf-02", "paper_id": "2011.07812", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The background is estimated with an ABCD method [ 79 ] by calculating the ratio of the number of events where lepton 1 passes inverted quality criteria (not including lepton $p_{\text{T}}$ or $|d_{0}|$ ) and lepton 2 passes nominal requirements, and vice versa, divided by the number of events where both leptons fail the quality criteria.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 3, "True": 3}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6", "Body ¶7 + Body ¶8 + Body ¶9 +  + Body ¶10 + Body ¶11 + Body ¶12 + Body ¶13"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention an ABCD method or any ABCD-style sideband or matrix method over independent regions.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention an ABCD method or any ABCD-style sideband or matrix method over independent regions.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention an ABCD method, an ABCD-style sideband or matrix method.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention an ABCD method, an ABCD-style sideband or matrix method.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention an ABCD method or any ABCD-style sideband or matrix method.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Body ¶1 + Body ¶2 + Body ¶3 + Body ¶4 + Body ¶5 + Body ¶6", "window": 0,