"escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The background is estimated with an ABCD method [ 79 ] by calculating the ratio of the number of events where lepton 1 passes inverted quality criteria (not including lepton $p_{\\text{T}}$ or $|d_{0}|$ ) and lepton 2 passes nominal requirements, and vice versa, divided by the number of events where both leptons fail the quality criteria.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly states that an ABCD method is used for background estimation.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": true, "quote": "The background is estimated with an ABCD method [ 79 ] by calculating the ratio of the number of events where lepton 1 passes inverted quality criteria (not including lepton $p_{\text{T}}$ or $|d_{0}|$ ) and lepton 2 passes nominal requirements, and vice versa, divided by the number of events where both leptons fail the quality criteria.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text explicitly states that the ABCD method is used to estimate the background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Body ¶7 + Body ¶8 + Body ¶9 +  + Body ¶10 + Body ¶11 + Body ¶12 + Body ¶13", "window": 1, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"yes\",\n  \"quote\": \"The background is estimated with an ABCD method [ 79 ] by calculating the ratio of the number of events where lepton 1 passes inverted quality criteria (not including lepton $p_{\\text{T}}$ or $|d_{0}|$ ) and lepton 2 passes nominal requirements, and vice versa, divided by the number of events where both leptons fail the quality criteria.\",\n  \"why\": \"The text explicitly states that the ABCD method is used to estimate the background.\"\n}\n```"}]}
