athup{{{W}}}}$ boson events + Selection of ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.4pt{\\mathup{{{c}}}}$ events", "window": 3, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Selection of ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}$ boson events + Selection of ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.4pt{\\mathup{{{c}}}}$ events", "window": 3, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SL channel", "window": 4, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The dominant background arises from ${{\\mathup{{{t}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}}$ production (around 8%), where one of the $\\mathup{{{W}}}$ bosons produced in the decay of the top quark pair decays leptonically and the other hadronically with a ${\\mathup{{{c}}}}$ quark in the final state.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions ttZ background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SL channel", "window": 4, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The dominant background arises from ${{\\mathup{{{t}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}}$ production (around 8%), where one of the $\\mathup{{{W}}}$ bosons produced in the decay of the top quark pair decays leptonically and the other hadronically with a ${\\mathup{{{c}}}}$ quark in the final state.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions ttZ production as a background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SL channel", "window": 4, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The dominant background arises from ${{\\mathup{{{t}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}}$ production (around 8%), where one of the $\\mathup{{{W}}}$ bosons produced in the decay of the top quark pair decays leptonically and the other hadronically with a ${\\mathup{{{c}}}}$ quark in the final state.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions ttZ production as a background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SV channel", "window": 5, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SV channel", "window": 5, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention a ttZ background or a control region used to normalise that background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection in the SV channel", "window": 5, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The dominant background comes from ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}+{{\\mathup{{{u}}}}{\\mathup{{{d}}}}{\\mathup{{{s}}}}{\\mathup{{{g}}}}}$ jets (around 15%), mostly from the processes ${{\\mathup{{{u}}}}{\\mathup{{{g}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{W}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}+{\\mathup{{{d}}}}}$ and ${{\\mathup{{{d}}}}{\\mathup{{{g}}}}\\to{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{W}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}+{\\mathup{{{u}}}}}$ , which are OS.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions a dominant background from ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}+{{\\mathup{{{u}}}}{\\mathup{{{d}}}}{\\mathup{{{s}}}}{\\mathup{{{g}}}}}$ jets.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "The uncertainty in the contribution from single top quark processes is estimated by varying the normalization of the samples according to the uncertainties in the theoretical cross sections, ~ 5–6% . It produces a negligible effect on the measurements.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions a ttZ background and a control region used to normalise that background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Systematic uncertainties", "window": 6, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The uncertainty in the contribution from single top quark processes is estimated by varying the normalization of the samples according to the uncertainties in the theoretical cross sections, ~ 5–6% . It produces a negligible effect on the measurements.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions a ttZ background and a control region used to normalise that background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "A ttZ-enriched control sample is selected by requiring a pair of high-pt isolated leptons of different flavour, e-, with opposite charge, following the same lepton selection criteria as in the W+c analysis.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text describes a ttZ-enriched control sample.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Systematic uncertainties", "window": 6, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"A ttZ-enriched control sample is selected by requiring a pair of high-pt isolated leptons of different flavour, e-, with opposite charge, following the same lepton selection criteria as in the W+c analysis.\", \"why\": \"The text describes a ttZ-enriched control sample.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2112.00895", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "A ttZ background is not mentioned.", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention a ttZ background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Systematic uncertainties", "window": 6, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"A ttZ background is not mentioned.\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention a ttZ background.\"}\n```"}]}
