, "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention the ABCD method or any ABCD-style sideband or matrix method.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and background prediction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention the ABCD method or any ABCD-style sideband or matrix method.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2012.01581", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and background prediction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The background yield in the signal region H can be estimated by different ratios of event counts in regions A–G, where the ratio $b_{\\mathrm{nominal}}=N_{ppf}(N_{ffp}+N_{fpp}+N_{pfp})/(N_{fff}+N_{pff}+N_{fpf})$ uses the fraction of events passing to those failing the GBDT selection (Selection 3) and is taken as the central value of the predicted background yields.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly describes using ratios of event counts in different regions to estimate the background yield.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2012.01581", "qid": "gf-02", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection and background prediction", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"yes\",\n  \"quote\": \"the background yield in the signal region H can be estimated by different ratios of event counts in regions A–G, where the ratio $b_{\\mathrm{nominal}}=N_{ppf}(N_{ffp}+N_{fpp}+N_{pfp})/(N_{fff}+N_{pff}+N_{fpf})$ uses the fraction of events passing to those failing the GBDT selection (Selection 3) and is taken as the central value of the predicted background yields.\",\n  \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions estimating the background yield using ratios of event counts in different regions.\"\n}\n```