{"qid": "gf-07", "paper_id": "2207.00348", "answer": null, "unanimous": false, "quote": "The analysis is furthermore specifically optimized for the detection of single-top associated production of the Higgs boson ( tH ), which has a unique sensitivity to the sign of the top-quark Yukawa coupling.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 11, "True": 1}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Introduction", "Modelling of the continuum background shape"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2207.00348", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Modelling of the continuum background shape", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"For categories targeting the $t\\overline{t}H$ and $tH$ processes, the diphoton events are primarily from $t\\bar{t}\\gamma\\gamma$ production.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions $t\\bar{t}\\gamma\\gamma$ production as the primary background for $t\\overline{t}H$ and $tH$ processes.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2207.00348", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Modelling of the continuum background shape", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"For categories targeting the $t\\overline{t}H$ and $tH$ processes, the diphoton events are primarily from $t\\bar{t}\\gamma\\gamma$ production. As such, a sample of simulated $t\\bar{t}\\gamma\\gamma$ events is used to construct the background template for those categories.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions $t\\bar{t}\\gamma\\gamma$ production as a background and the use of a simulated sample to construct the background template.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2207.00348", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Modelling of the continuum background shape", "window": 0, "escalated": false, 