{"qid": "gf-07", "paper_id": "2407.10549", "answer": null, "unanimous": false, "quote": "Backgrounds from associated $Vh$ production were generated at NLO in QCD with Powheg Box interfaced to Pythia  8.186 using the NNPDF3.0 NLO PDF set.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 1, "True": 2}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": ["Simulation of signal and background processes"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2407.10549", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention a control region used to normalize the ttZ background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Simulation of signal and background processes", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention a control region used to normalize the ttZ background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2407.10549", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "Backgrounds from associated $Vh$ production were generated at NLO in QCD with Powheg Box interfaced to Pythia  8.186 using the NNPDF3.0 NLO PDF set.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions the generation of ttZ background.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Simulation of signal and background processes", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"yes\",\n  \"quote\": \"Backgrounds from associated $Vh$ production were generated at NLO in QCD with Powheg Box interfaced to Pythia  8.186 using the NNPDF3.0 NLO PDF set.\",\n  \"why\": \"The text mentions the generation of ttZ background.\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2407.10549", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": true, "quote": "The $t\bar{t}$ samples were normalized using calculations at NNLO in QCD including next-to-next-to-leading logarithmic soft-gluon terms calculated using Top++  2.0 [ 84 , 85 , 86 , 87 , 88 , 89 , 90 ] .", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions normalization of tt samples", "answer_text": "", "section": "Simulation of signal and background processes", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The $t\\bar{t}$ samples were normalized using calculations at NNLO in QCD including next-to-next-to-leading logarithmic soft-gluon terms calculated using Top++  2.0 [ 84 , 85 , 86 , 87 , 88 , 89 , 90 ] .\", \"why\": \"The text mentions normalization of tt samples\"}\n```"}]}
