{"qid": "gf-07", "paper_id": "2506.13565", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The systematic uncertainty in the tt estimation is derived from the deviations observed in the tt VR in data and simulation after applying the DNN selection.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 24, "True": 3}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector", "Background estimation", "Event selection", "Object reconstruction", "Signal models + Event simulation", "Systematic uncertainties"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2506.13565", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Background estimation", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ CR is obtained by selecting an oppositely charged, different-flavor lepton pair ( ${\\mathup{{{e}}}}{\\mathup{}}$ ), where all the selection criteria for the ${\\mathup{{{e}}}}$ and are kept the same as to those in the SR with $m_{{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}}>200\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ , except no DNN score selection is applied in this region.\", \"why\": \"The text describes a control region used to derive a scale factor for the ttZ background.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2506.13565", "qid": "gf-07", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Background estimation", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ CR is obtained by selecting an oppositely charged, different-flavor lepton pair ( ${\\mathup{{{e}}}}{\\mathup{}}$ ), where all the selection criteria for the ${\\mathup{{{e}}}}$ and are kept the same as to those in the SR with $m_{{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}{\\mathup{{{\\ell}}}}}>200\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ , except no DNN score selecti