s separate regions.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2011.07812", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": true, "quote": "SR-ee and SR-mumu are fit individually to calculate limits on GMSB SUSY models with a tilde{e} or tilde{mu} NLSP, while tilde{tau} NLSP and co-NLSP limits are obtained using a simultaneous fit of all three signal regions.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions fitting SR-ee and SR-mumu individually, indicating parallel ee and mumu channels.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Body ¶14 +  + Body ¶15 + Body ¶16 + Body ¶17 + Body ¶18 + Body ¶19 + Body ¶20", "window": 2, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"SR-ee and SR-mumu are fit individually to calculate limits on GMSB SUSY models with a tilde{e} or tilde{mu} NLSP, while tilde{tau} NLSP and co-NLSP limits are obtained using a simultaneous fit of all three signal regions.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions fitting SR-ee and SR-mumu individually, indicating parallel ee and mumu channels.\"}\n```"}]}
