two electrons or exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The signal includes three distinct channels: two same-flavor channels corresponding to two electrons ( ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ ) or two muons ( ${\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ ), and the different-flavor channel corresponding to one electron and one muon ( ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\pm}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{\\mp}}}}$ ).\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions two same-flavor channels: one for two electrons and one for two muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events are selected offline if they contain exactly two isolated, oppositely charged electrons or muons, ( ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ , ${\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ , ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\pm}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{\\mp}}}}$ )\", \"why\": \"The text specifies that events are selected if they contain exactly two isolated, oppositely charged electrons or muons, indicating parallel ee and mumu channels.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Events are selected offline if they contain exactly two isolated, oppositely charged electrons or muons, ( ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ , ${\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ , ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{\\pm}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{\\mp}}}}$ )\", \"why\": \"The text specifies that events are selected if they contain exactly two isolated, oppositely charged electrons or muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic reconstruction of the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ system", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic reconstruction of the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ system", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Kinematic reconstruction of the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ system", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": true, "quote": "The data were recorded with the CMS detector at the CERN Large Hadron Collider and correspond to an integrated luminosity of 138 fb−1.", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The analysis uses events containing two oppositely charged leptons, which can be either electrons or muons.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The data were recorded with the CMS detector at the CERN Large Hadron Collider and correspond to an integrated luminosity of 138 fb−1.\", \"why\": \"The analysis uses events containing two oppositely charged leptons, which can be either electrons or muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2402.08486", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Differential cross sections for top quark pair ( $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ ) production are measured in proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of 13 TeV using a sample of events containing two oppositely charged leptons.\", \"why\": \"The text specifies 'two oppositely charged leptons' without specifying the type of leptons.\"}\n```"}]}
{"qid": "gf-08", "paper_id": "2401.07090", "answer": null, "unanimous": false, "quote": "In the electron channel, in order to increase the purity of the sample, we require at least one of the electrons to be reconstructed with the PF algorithm.", "answers": [], "votes": {"False": 25, "True": 2}, "escalated": true, "sections_read": [" + Abstract + Introduction", "Event reconstruction and selection", "Event simulation", "Measurement strategy", "The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples + $\\mathup{{{B}}}$ parking data sample", "The CMS detector + Event simulation"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention the selection of exactly two electrons or exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Event simulation", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention the selection of exactly two electrons or exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention any selection criteria for electrons or muons.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Event simulation", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention any selection criteria for electrons or muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention any selection criteria for electrons or muons.", "answer_text": "", "section": "The CMS detector + Event simulation", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not mention any selection criteria for electrons or muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction and selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"yes\",\n  \"quote\": \"The $\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{B}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}$ candidates are formed using a pair of opposite-sign (OS) same-flavor leptons with an invariant mass below $5\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and a positively charged track, to which the kaon mass is assigned.\",\n  \"why\": \"The text specifies that the analysis forms B+ candidates using a pair of opposite-sign same-flavor leptons, which includes both electrons and muons.\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction and selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"To measure $R({\\mathup{{{K}}}})$ , we select events for which either a ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{B}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}\\!\\to\\!{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{K}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ candidate (used in the numerator of the $R({\\mathup{{{K}}}})$ ratio) is found on the tag side, i.e., a muon from the ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{B}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}\\!\\to\\!{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{K}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ candidate must satisfy the trigger conditions, or a ${\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{B}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}\\!\\to\\!{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{K}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{+}}}}{\\mathup{{{{\\mathup{{{e}}}}}}^{\\scriptstyle{-}}}}$ candidate (used in the denominator of the $R({\\mathup{{{K}}}})$ ratio) is found on the probe side.\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions selecting events with either a muon or electron pair, indicating parallel ee and mumu channels.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not explicitly state that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction and selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not explicitly state that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction and selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The muon, PF-PF, and PF-LP channels are then combined statistically for the $R({\\mathup{{{K}}}})$ extraction.\", \"why\": \"The text mentions muon and electron channels separately and combines them statistically.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction and selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.07090", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not mention selecting events with exactly two muons as an alternative to exactly two electrons.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Event reconstruction and selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \