se, "reasoning": "The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Fiducial-volume definition + Background estimation + Irreducible backgrounds + $VV$ and $t\\bar{t}Z/\\gamma^{*}$ backgrounds + Other irreducible backgrounds + Reducible backgrounds", "window": 6, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.05299", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Fiducial-volume definition + Background estimation + Irreducible backgrounds + $VV$ and $t\\bar{t}Z/\\gamma^{*}$ backgrounds + Other irreducible backgrounds + Reducible backgrounds", "window": 6, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.05299", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Fiducial-volume definition + Background estimation + Irreducible backgrounds + $VV$ and $t\\bar{t}Z/\\gamma^{*}$ backgrounds + Other irreducible backgrounds + Reducible backgrounds", "window": 6, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"no\", \"quote\": \"\", \"why\": \"The text does not specify that the analysis requires exactly two electrons OR exactly two muons as alternative selections.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.05299", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": true, "quote": "Several of the event categories introduced in Section Analysis strategy were designed to be enriched in specific processes and are used to derive normalisation factors to improve the modelling in the simulation. The 3ℓ MatC CR is enriched in material conversions (denoted as “Mat Conv”) and only the total event yield is used. There are six 2ℓ CRs enriched in contributions from HF non-prompt leptons in tt events, i.e. 2ℓ tt(e) TMex , 2ℓ tt(e) MexT , 2ℓ tt(e) MexMex , 2ℓ tt(μ) TMex , 2ℓ tt(μ) MexT , and 2ℓ tt(μ) MexMex .", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text mentions six 2ℓ CRs, three with electrons and three with muons.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Non-prompt leptons + Charge misassignment + Systematic uncertainties + Instrumental uncertainties", "window": 7, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Several of the event categories introduced in Section Analysis strategy were designed to be enriched in specific processes and are used to derive normalisation factors to improve the modelling in the simulation. The 3ℓ MatC CR is enriched in material conversions (denoted as “Mat Conv”) and only the total event yield is used. There are six 2ℓ CRs enriched in contributions from HF non-prompt leptons in tt events, i.e. 2ℓ tt(e) TMex , 2ℓ tt(e) MexT , 2ℓ tt(e) MexMex , 2ℓ tt(μ) TMex , 2ℓ tt(μ) MexT , and 2ℓ tt(μ) MexMex .\", \"why\": \"The text mentions six 2ℓ CRs, three with electrons and three with muons.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.05299", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": true, "quote": "Several of the event categories introduced in Section Analysis strategy were designed to be enriched in specific processes and are used to derive normalisation factors to improve the modelling in the simulation. The 3ℓ MatC CR is enriched in material conversions (denoted as “Mat Conv”) and only the total event yield is used. There are six 2ℓ CRs enriched in contributions from HF non-prompt leptons in tt¯ events, i.e. 2ℓ tt(e) TMex , 2ℓ tt(e) MexT , 2ℓ tt(e) MexMex , 2ℓ tt(μ) TMex , 2ℓ tt(μ) MexT , and 2ℓ tt(μ) MexMex .", "quote_verified": true, "reasoning": "The text explicitly mentions six 2ℓ CRs enriched in contributions from HF non-prompt leptons in tt¯ events, including both electron and muon channels.", "answer_text": "", "section": "Non-prompt leptons + Charge misassignment + Systematic uncertainties + Instrumental uncertainties", "window": 7, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"Several of the event categories introduced in Section Analysis strategy were designed to be enriched in specific processes and are used to derive normalisation factors to improve the modelling in the simulation. The 3ℓ MatC CR is enriched in material conversions (denoted as “Mat Conv”) and only the total event yield is used. There are six 2ℓ CRs enriched in contributions from HF non-prompt leptons in tt¯ events, i.e. 2ℓ tt(e) TMex , 2ℓ tt(e) MexT , 2ℓ tt(e) MexMex , 2ℓ tt(μ) TMex , 2ℓ tt(μ) MexT , and 2ℓ tt(μ) MexMex .\", \"why\": \"The text explicitly mentions six 2ℓ CRs enriched in contributions from HF non-prompt leptons in tt¯ events, including both electron and muon channels.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2401.05299", "qid": "gf-08", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Non-prompt leptons + Charge misassignment + Systematic uncertainties + Instrumental uncertainties", "window": 7, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"There are six $2\\ell$ CRs enriched in contributions from HF non-prompt leptons in $t\\bar{t}$ events, i.e. $2\\ell$ tt(e) ${}_{TM_{\\mathrm{ex}}}$ , $2\\ell$ tt(e) ${}_{M_{\\mathrm{ex}}T}$ , $2\\ell$ tt(e) ${}_{M_{\\mathrm{ex}}M_{\\mathrm{ex}}}$ , $2\\ell$ tt( $\\mu$ ) ${}_{TM_{\\mathrm{ex}}}$ , $2\\ell$ tt( $\\mu$ ) ${}_{M_{\\mathrm{ex}}T}$ , and $2\\ell$ tt( $\\mu$ ) ${}_{M_{\\mathrm{ex}}M_{\\mathrm{ex}}}$ .\", \"why\": \"The text mentions specific control regions for electrons and muons separately.\"}\n```"}]}
