does not unfold its measured distributions.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2404.06204", "qid": "gf-04", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + The ATLAS detector and datasets + ATLAS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"yes\",\n  \"quote\": \"For $W$ bosons, the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ spectrum is primarily measured through the transverse momentum of the charged decay leptons.\",\n  \"why\": \"The text says the analysis does this.\"\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2404.06204", "qid": "gf-04", "answer": true, "quote": "The $p_{\text{T}}^{W}$ distributions are corrected for detector effects by unfolding the measured distributions using a response matrix and the regularized unfolding method.", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "The sentence explicitly states that the analysis corrects for detector effects by unfolding the measured distributions.", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + The ATLAS detector and datasets + ATLAS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"quote\": \"The $p_{\\text{T}}^{W}$ distributions are corrected for detector effects by unfolding the measured distributions using a response matrix and the regularized unfolding method.\", \"why\": \"The sentence explicitly states that the analysis corrects for detector effects by unfolding the measured distributions.\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2404.06204", "qid": "gf-04", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction + The ATLAS detector and datasets + ATLAS detector", "window": 0, "escalated": true, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"yes\",\n  \"quote\": \"For $W\\rightarrow\\ell\\nu$ events, the measured distributions are unfolded to particle level using a regularized unfolding procedure.\",\n  \"why\": \"The text explicitly states that the measured distributions are unfolded.\